1
00:00:29,905 --> 00:00:31,198
FUN AMUSEMENT PARK

2
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:37,496
{\an8}REMOTE AR MEETING
GUICHENG - ACADEMY

3
00:00:43,085 --> 00:00:46,046
<i>Naozumi.</i>

4
00:00:48,716 --> 00:00:52,720
<i>When will you finally find Nagi?</i>

5
00:00:55,473 --> 00:00:56,724
I'm terribly sorry.

6
00:00:57,933 --> 00:01:00,519
We're always just one step away...

7
00:01:02,313 --> 00:01:06,609
But then he disappears
as if he knew our every move...

8
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:09,779
<i>Hmm.</i>

9
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:25,544
<i>By the way...</i>

10
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:30,883
<i>Who are you?</i>

11
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:18,573
Hmm... It'll probably be just enough...

12
00:03:18,574 --> 00:03:19,408
FAN CLUB MEMBERS

13
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,334
What's wrong, Doc?

14
00:03:39,553 --> 00:03:44,099
Your Sensei noticed
they were being watched.

15
00:03:50,356 --> 00:03:53,984
We probably won't be able to use
my "eyes" to keep tabs on them anymore.

16
00:03:57,112 --> 00:04:02,409
I'd heard the rumors, but they're
a monster beyond anything I imagined.

17
00:04:04,495 --> 00:04:05,454
Yeah...

18
00:04:10,793 --> 00:04:11,710
Indeed,

19
00:04:12,962 --> 00:04:15,005
if you're going to take them on,

20
00:04:16,674 --> 00:04:18,842
I suppose the No Mark
is your only chance...

21
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:22,680
Let's hurry up and finish it.

22
00:04:32,022 --> 00:04:37,236
<i>Looks like one of Nagi's friends
can control animals.</i>

23
00:04:37,903 --> 00:04:39,029
<i>Didn't you notice?</i>

24
00:04:45,661 --> 00:04:49,415
<i>Perhaps promoting
you two siblings to Class A</i>

25
00:04:50,374 --> 00:04:52,334
<i>was a mistake after all.</i>

26
00:05:02,886 --> 00:05:06,015
<i>Maybe you're nothing
but "defective vessels" after all...</i>

27
00:05:22,573 --> 00:05:25,324
Me! Me! Me!

28
00:05:25,325 --> 00:05:26,452
Here!

29
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:29,204
<i>Yes, Uzu?</i>

30
00:05:29,496 --> 00:05:30,372
Yes!

31
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:34,167
I tracked down the whereabouts
of the Tahira siblings

32
00:05:34,168 --> 00:05:38,047
through my own channels!

33
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:40,966
- What?! You never told us--
<i>- Enough.</i>

34
00:05:43,552 --> 00:05:44,636
<i>Shut up.</i>

35
00:05:49,641 --> 00:05:50,642
<i>Go on.</i>

36
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,687
Ever since I arrived on this island,

37
00:05:53,812 --> 00:05:58,567
I've been taking down
every strong guy I could find.

38
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:03,280
And making as big a spectacle
of it as possible.

39
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:08,576
Guicheng is a legal vacuum
ruled by violence.

40
00:06:08,577 --> 00:06:10,412
The fastest way to gather information

41
00:06:10,996 --> 00:06:16,502
is to show everyone
how strong I am, I figured.

42
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:21,256
Plus, that means a smaller supply
of "medicine" for Nagi.

43
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:24,093
<i>Good thinking.</i>

44
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:27,137
<i>Everything finds its way</i>

45
00:06:28,055 --> 00:06:31,683
<i>to those with power.</i>

46
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:36,646
Yes! After that, my informants
started prioritizing me

47
00:06:36,647 --> 00:06:40,526
when passing along information.

48
00:06:47,032 --> 00:06:52,329
That's how I found out
about a new underground organization.

49
00:06:52,955 --> 00:06:56,582
Most of its members
are street kids from Guicheng.

50
00:06:56,583 --> 00:07:02,840
All they do is steal supplies
and stuff. Nothing major...

51
00:07:03,757 --> 00:07:07,094
But their group's symbol caught my eye...

52
00:07:07,636 --> 00:07:08,428
PROJECTION MODE

53
00:07:08,804 --> 00:07:09,680
Here it is.

54
00:07:11,265 --> 00:07:15,894
Doesn't it look like a wheelchair...?

55
00:07:18,313 --> 00:07:22,651
I've also heard they're "building
something" down in the underground levels.

56
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:27,406
I think it's worth investigating.

57
00:07:31,660 --> 00:07:34,371
<i>Yes, I agree.</i>

58
00:07:37,207 --> 00:07:41,295
<i>Starting today, Uzu will be
in charge of this operation.</i>

59
00:07:43,130 --> 00:07:46,258
Yes, sir! Thank you so much!

60
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:59,563
<i>This bastard... He kept the information
to himself</i>

61
00:08:00,063 --> 00:08:03,025
<i>just to impress Sensei.</i>

62
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:07,362
<i>All right, keep up the good work.</i>

63
00:08:08,989 --> 00:08:10,741
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

64
00:08:12,284 --> 00:08:13,202
<i>Uzu.</i>

65
00:08:14,328 --> 00:08:16,288
<i>You know, that present...</i>

66
00:08:16,997 --> 00:08:19,625
<i>Make sure you deliver it.</i>

67
00:08:19,791 --> 00:08:21,084
END OF TRANSMISSION

68
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,212
<i>Ding-dong!</i>

69
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:28,800
<i>If you want another ride,
please insert 100 yen.</i>

70
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:41,146
How scary! Don't get mad at me.

71
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:45,567
We're in Class A. It's only natural
for us to have secrets!

72
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:55,827
What's this "present"?

73
00:08:55,953 --> 00:08:57,955
Oh! That's right!

74
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:02,626
Sensei told me to give it to Touko senpai
when they gave me the signal.

75
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:05,504
To Touko...?

76
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,925
Oh, here it is!

77
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:17,599
What's this?

78
00:09:18,016 --> 00:09:19,685
Gas canister No. 5.

79
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:24,731
Touko senpai can use gas
to enhance her body.

80
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:28,860
This is a special new formula
made by the science club.

81
00:09:29,361 --> 00:09:32,239
It'll kill her if she uses it,
but it's suuuper effective!

82
00:09:35,826 --> 00:09:36,702
Huh?

83
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:38,996
What?

84
00:09:40,372 --> 00:09:43,000
Ah... Ah... okay...

85
00:09:44,042 --> 00:09:47,587
Sensei entrusted it to me, so--

86
00:09:47,754 --> 00:09:49,006
Not that...

87
00:09:53,635 --> 00:09:54,511
"It'll kill her"?

88
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:56,763
Huh? Yeah, it'll kill her if she uses it.

89
00:10:00,267 --> 00:10:04,354
But, man, I'm jealous...

90
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:11,153
Getting a present from Sensei...

91
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:12,362
It'll...

92
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:16,658
It'll... kill her...

93
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:34,885
I'll hold on to this.

94
00:10:37,804 --> 00:10:41,433
I'll decide when to use it.

95
00:10:54,488 --> 00:10:57,949
{\an8}THREE YEARS AGO

96
00:10:58,492 --> 00:11:02,162
BULLETIN BOARD

97
00:11:04,748 --> 00:11:06,166
4 TOUKO KUROSAKA

98
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:08,418
27 NAOZUMI KUROSAKA

99
00:11:18,136 --> 00:11:19,012
<i>Touko.</i>

100
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:23,183
<i>You're asking if I'm really going through
with the octopus surgery?</i>

101
00:11:24,601 --> 00:11:26,353
<i>We've gone over this already.</i>

102
00:11:30,065 --> 00:11:31,691
<i>I know the risks.</i>

103
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:38,365
<i>But I have to get stronger
if I'm going to survive here.</i>

104
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:41,576
Especially...

105
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:44,830
when I have something precious
to protect...

106
00:11:56,216 --> 00:11:57,217
<i>What did you say?</i>

107
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:03,348
I'll protect you,

108
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:08,311
big brother.

109
00:12:10,397 --> 00:12:12,649
<i>After undergoing
the "Migraine Mollusk" surgery,</i>

110
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:17,946
<i>I returned home after six months
of hellish rehab, and waiting for me...</i>

111
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:23,368
<i>was Touko, who had undergone body
augmentation surgery without my knowledge.</i>

112
00:12:40,177 --> 00:12:42,179
<i>Is this really our only choice?</i>

113
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:23,512
<i>I'm so close...</i>

114
00:13:24,638 --> 00:13:27,641
<i>All I need is one last push,</i>

115
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:33,146
<i>and I'll become "perfect."</i>

116
00:14:45,927 --> 00:14:48,930
It's been a while, Nagi.

117
00:14:50,682 --> 00:14:53,268
I was expecting you.

118
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:55,729
You...

119
00:14:57,731 --> 00:15:00,483
wanted to talk to me, too, didn't you?

120
00:15:02,777 --> 00:15:05,488
This kind of parapsychic sharing

121
00:15:06,406 --> 00:15:08,867
only works

122
00:15:09,576 --> 00:15:11,411
if both parties want to communicate.

123
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:16,333
I suppose you're right.

124
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:34,684
What are you doing?

125
00:15:35,852 --> 00:15:37,020
How tragic...

126
00:15:39,397 --> 00:15:41,900
Your unique constitution
makes your body stronger

127
00:15:43,902 --> 00:15:46,696
the more killing intent you're exposed to.

128
00:15:47,572 --> 00:15:49,449
Under normal circumstances,

129
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:53,578
you should be able to recover
from any injury instantly.

130
00:15:55,163 --> 00:15:56,581
And yet,

131
00:15:57,999 --> 00:16:02,921
your consciousness and body

132
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:06,633
are unable to fully recover.

133
00:16:07,926 --> 00:16:12,514
The bullet lodged in your brainstem,
the core of your ability,

134
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:16,685
is preventing it from activating.

135
00:16:18,228 --> 00:16:20,021
That thing in the sky

136
00:16:21,189 --> 00:16:24,359
is an image of the bullet
still lodged in your brain.

137
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:30,615
Someone as skilled as you

138
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:34,452
shouldn't have suffered
such an injury so easily.

139
00:16:36,287 --> 00:16:38,039
Unless...

140
00:16:39,958 --> 00:16:41,918
you were protecting someone.

141
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:47,674
So she really is a curse to you...

142
00:16:49,384 --> 00:16:51,845
I should have gotten rid of her sooner.

143
00:16:55,432 --> 00:16:56,766
Sensei.

144
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,394
I left the Academy

145
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:03,106
because you tried to kill Shizuka.

146
00:17:05,442 --> 00:17:06,359
Please,

147
00:17:07,736 --> 00:17:09,988
just leave us alone.

148
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:13,324
Nagi.

149
00:17:15,076 --> 00:17:16,161
It's not too late.

150
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:20,749
If you accept
my "ultimate killing intent,"

151
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,877
you might not only return to normal,

152
00:17:24,836 --> 00:17:27,338
but even become "perfect."

153
00:17:30,550 --> 00:17:32,135
Come back to me.

154
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:36,264
When you say "perfect,"

155
00:17:37,932 --> 00:17:41,311
you mean becoming
someone just like you, don't you?

156
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:44,397
Sensei,

157
00:17:46,483 --> 00:17:47,984
what are you, really?

158
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:52,030
"Sensei."

159
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:56,576
"The One Who Lives On."

160
00:17:57,994 --> 00:18:02,040
I've been called many things
over the years,

161
00:18:02,957 --> 00:18:03,917
but none

162
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:08,588
have described me quite so well.

163
00:18:12,425 --> 00:18:14,469
Where should I begin...

164
00:18:26,523 --> 00:18:27,398
Hm?

165
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:31,027
That's going back a bit too far.

166
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:32,904
Let's see...

167
00:18:34,823 --> 00:18:36,157
Basically,

168
00:18:36,908 --> 00:18:38,660
at first,

169
00:18:39,369 --> 00:18:41,162
everything was wonderful.

170
00:18:42,455 --> 00:18:46,501
Back when everything was new...

171
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:59,180
But gradually, I came to understand.

172
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:03,351
The people around me

173
00:19:04,519 --> 00:19:06,771
look like me,

174
00:19:07,856 --> 00:19:09,357
but they are very different.

175
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:12,151
They are "imperfect beings."

176
00:19:14,946 --> 00:19:17,115
Their wounds don't heal instantly.

177
00:19:18,324 --> 00:19:19,868
They need to sleep.

178
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:26,040
They can lift, at most, about five times
their own body weight.

179
00:19:28,293 --> 00:19:31,546
They can't hear a pin
drop a kilometer away.

180
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:37,594
They can't have children with me.

181
00:19:39,429 --> 00:19:42,223
They can only see a narrow range

182
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:44,684
of electromagnetic wavelengths.

183
00:19:46,603 --> 00:19:47,562
And...

184
00:19:49,939 --> 00:19:51,274
eventually, they die.

185
00:19:54,527 --> 00:20:01,034
I've spent my life searching everywhere,

186
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:07,957
under every possible title,
for others like myself.

187
00:20:10,335 --> 00:20:14,964
King, count, <i>kitsune</i>...

188
00:20:16,382 --> 00:20:21,679
Boss, party leader, cult leader...

189
00:20:23,556 --> 00:20:24,432
God...

190
00:20:26,267 --> 00:20:27,226
Demon...

191
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:33,232
Even creating the Academy
and gathering children there

192
00:20:34,192 --> 00:20:37,528
was all for that purpose.

193
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:40,865
And then, ten years ago...

194
00:20:43,910 --> 00:20:46,037
I finally found one.

195
00:20:52,919 --> 00:20:56,089
A child who could have
my physical abilities,

196
00:20:57,215 --> 00:21:01,344
but only when someone
directs killing intent at them.

197
00:21:03,304 --> 00:21:06,933
A "vessel" capable of becoming "perfect."

198
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:11,145
In other words, you.

199
00:21:19,988 --> 00:21:20,947
I see...

200
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:28,204
Nagi,

201
00:21:30,581 --> 00:21:34,043
I haven't given up.

202
00:21:36,004 --> 00:21:39,382
Next time, let's meet in person.

203
00:21:50,268 --> 00:21:54,397
<i>Sensei's killing intent might
even be able to heal your body.</i>

204
00:21:58,943 --> 00:22:00,695
What should I do?

205
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,076
Even if...

206
00:22:10,538 --> 00:22:11,998
it means being imperfect,

207
00:22:14,625 --> 00:22:15,752
I'd rather be human.

208
00:23:58,062 --> 00:24:01,065
{\an8}SUBTITLES BY FRANCESCA BOARA

